{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216692-what-would-a-tokusatsu-character-be-in-the-exalted-setting","id":1216692,"title":"What would a Tokusatsu character be in the Exalted setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-08T09:05:53-07:00","id":1216692,"title":"What would a Tokusatsu character be in the Exalted setting","content":"Series including: Kamen Rider, Super Sentai, Ultraman, GARO<br /> <br /> Example: GARO-Solar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:38:37-07:00","id":1216706,"title":"","content":"Ultraman... I feel like that's hard to represent outside of just giving someone an Ultraman-themed Warstrider?<br /> <br /> Kamen Rider... exact Exalt type would be individual (especially if you're looking at canon Riders), but I'd argue that a Kamen Rider could be represented by an Exalt with a special suit of artifact armor, wherein the armor is stored in Elsewhere and can be drawn out by the artifact belt.<br /> <br /> Sentai often get comparisons from five-Aspected Dragon-Blooded teams, especially when each is in corresponding Jade armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T10:01:06-07:00","id":1216718,"title":"","content":"Strictly speaking a sentai or kamen rider - a normal human who derives powers from a transformation that grants them some sort of suit - would be a gunzosha. <br /> <br /> Or an exigent whose powers manifest as some sort of transformation. They'd have limited access to magic in their non-transformed state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T10:38:53-07:00","id":1216733,"title":"","content":"Bug-totemed Lunars can assume hybrid forms with exoskeleton armor plating. Very Kamen Rider and Bio-Booster Armor Guyver. If you\u2019re a Full Moon, your Caste Mark will even look like a Guyver\u2019s control metal, if any tattoos on your forehead doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Then the Lunar uses the \u201cI become a giant me\u201d Charm, so now he\u2019s Ultraman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T12:31:20-07:00","id":1216768,"title":"","content":"Back in 2e I would have actually suggested a rebellious Infernal or Renegade Abyssal for Kamen Rider, since a common theme in those series is the heroes' power having some kind of relationship to the primary villains of the season (especially in Showa, where the hero was often outright made into a Rider by the villains). I'm less sure of that these days since Abyssals are leaving behind the master/slave relationship with the Deathlords and Infernals are gonna be something completely different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T02:33:01-07:00","id":1216938,"title":"","content":"I just remembered Blue Beetle was a thing. Do you think the Scarab would work better as a strange physical exigence or just some funky artifact that's basically Super-Gunzosha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T04:02:32-07:00","id":1216943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216692-what-would-a-tokusatsu-character-be-in-the-exalted-setting?p=1216938#post1216938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just remembered Blue Beetle was a thing. Do you think the Scarab would work better as a strange physical exigence or just some funky artifact that's basically Super-Gunzosha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Tricky, this one, since I can see both as options. If we're looking to emulate it being at odds with its host, I'd lean towards powerful sentient artifact... although, could a god end up copying their mind onto the Exigence?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T18:34:15-07:00","id":1221901,"title":"","content":"Maybe i'm a little prejudiced against the color-coded quintets, but - parallels with dragon-blooded division by 5 elements/colors notwithstanding - Super Sentai in general don't really make me think of Exalted. More like mortals that lucked out in getting artifacts that work and open a few evocations for them.<br /> <br /> For Ultraman, i would suggest looking into Mela's Coil from Arms of the Chosen, specially its pinnacle evocation, that let's the wearer turn into an elemental dragon (modeled on Fakharu's stats).<br /> <br /> Beans' points about the older Kamen Riders originating as rogue projects of the villains makes me think that a &quot;Black Market Exigence&quot; might go pretty well with this theme in 3e, maybe even better in replicating the Gorgon Group than an Abyssal or Infernal's connection to their respective masters would.<br /> <br /> GARO i have heard about and seen bits, but don't know well enough to comment about. Remember it vaguely as a tokusatsu centered on a Dante-esque (from Devil May Cry) hero dealing with weird threats ripped from J-horror with some Hellraiser mixed in? At least until some golden eyesore armor kind of ruined it for me, i guess. So much promise anihilated by the cringe of one awful piece of CGI. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-20-2021, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}